# Design system sync

When you change **visual UI** (layout, copy, colours, typography, spacing, interaction states, or new screens), update the design system in the **same change** unless the user explicitly says to skip it.

## Production → preview mapping

| Production surface | Shared component(s) | Design-system preview |
|--------------------|---------------------|------------------------|
| `/control` | `ControlPanel`, `MatchConfirmation` | `/design-system/preview/control?state=` |
| `/setup`, `/playing` | `SetupDisplay`, `PlayingDisplay`, `MatchConfirmation` | `/design-system/preview/setup?state=`, `/playing?state=` |
| Court TV | `CourtDisplay` | `/design-system/preview/court?state=` + `court-preview-states.ts` |
| Spectator TV | `SpectatorDisplay` | `/design-system/preview/spectator?state=` |
| `/session-review` | `SessionReviewDisplay` | `/design-system/preview/session-review` |
| `/game/[id]` | `GameDetailDisplay` | `/design-system/preview/game` |
| Matchplay | matchplay pages | `/design-system/preview/matchplay?state=` |

Hub tabs live in `app/design-system/screens/**` (e.g. `PlayerMobileHub.tsx`, `court/page.tsx`). Add or relabel tabs when a new state or route is user-visible.

## How to stay in sync

1. **Prefer shared display components** — previews should render the same component as production with a `preview` prop or mock data, not duplicate markup.
2. **New screen state** — extend the relevant `*-preview-config.ts` / `*-preview-states.ts` and add a hub tab in `ScreenPreview` states.
3. **CSS / tokens** — if you change shared classes (`.preview-*`, `.session-review-*`, `.player-flow-*`, tokens in `app/styles/tokens/`), check component showcase pages under `/design-system/components/*` and foundations pages when tokens change.
4. **Player flow shell** — gate/loading screens use `PlayerFlowShell` + `SessionPromptCard`; keep `/setup`, `/playing`, and staff `/control` loading/error states aligned.
5. **Temporary flags** (e.g. `SESSION_REVIEW_GAME_NAV_ENABLED`) — previews using the same component inherit behaviour; document in preview page comment if non-obvious.
6. **Mock data** — keep `app/design-system/lib/*-preview-data.ts` aligned with preview states (names, scores, branding via `squareone-mock-branding.ts`).

## Before finishing

- [ ] Identified which preview route(s) mirror the changed UI
- [ ] Updated preview config, mock data, or hub tabs if needed
- [ ] Did not leave production-only markup that previews no longer exercise

Reference: `docs/design-system-audit.md` for route inventory.
